{"title":"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Chun and Rashid share a rectangular garden. The ratio of the area of Chun’s portion to the area of Rashid’s portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e47d95347d6e72d1b3e8a4aea3dd20082f3cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3:2$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />. They each plant daisies and tulips on their portion of the garden. On Chun’s portion of the garden, the ratio of the area covered by daisies to the area covered by tulips is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3714d1977e2e6fa2c03536bd04eabab371fd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If half of the area of the entire garden is covered by daisies and half is covered by tulips, what is the ratio of the area covered by daisies to the area covered by tulips on Rashid’s portion?\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Using_a_Value.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Using_a_Value)\">Solution 1 (Using a Value)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Using a Value)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To make the problem easier, we can select a value for the total area covered by the garden. We can say that the total area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which makes the area of Chun's portion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9fab845152f9501ac753c9a965fa4810ee96711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20}{5} \\times 3 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" /> and the area of Rashid's portion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45d82a1582e711a5eae47ce022369ab9c9aa4783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - 12 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Additionally, half of the area of the whole field is covered by tulips and half the area of the whole field is covered by daisies, so the area covered by each flower is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec50d1c6a800c1ef2931eeb78ad1a26c0fb2dd0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{20}{2} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The ratio of the area of the daisies on Chun's portion to the area of the tulips on Chun's portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3714d1977e2e6fa2c03536bd04eabab371fd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, so this means that the area covered by the daisies on his side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b6d1536cf5df8ece99bd37d2c814f4acb36faec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{3} \\times 2 = 4 \\times 2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The total area for the daisies is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the area covered by the daisies on Rashid's portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/569416017a32eb367d4726d3737ae6b1013a0901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - 8 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. This means that the area covered by the tulips on Rashid's portion would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7562f0b1f5a12fe433a351503500202a9426134a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 - 2 = 6$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the ratio of the number of daisies to the number of tulips on Rashid's portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd07ba1593a028644778cfbe3eda27010c499626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:6$\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, which reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08da6a3aafa43c2360496bc38f9073fd173be063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"46\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the total area covered by the garden. This means that the area of Chun's portion would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec815fc43fe755796d8075168cc2ad66795e2f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> and the area of Rashid's portion would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffc11e5ab40899d3cb1b1437b53b3109ada7d731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />. Additionally, half of the total area is covered by each flower, so the tulips and daisies would each cover <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a9e26de4f987e24345a7279e91cdce518c074b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The ratio of the area of the daisies on Chun's portion to the area of the tulips on Chun's portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3714d1977e2e6fa2c03536bd04eabab371fd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, so this means that the area covered by the tulips is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b1c8ff9b29e3a81be6a22fa7e90a9c17a706f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{5}x = \\frac{1}{5}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The total area covered by the tulips is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a9e26de4f987e24345a7279e91cdce518c074b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />, so the area covered by the tulips on Rashid's portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53fcc5a5aa955e91be6f3100761646e0f544815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}x - \\frac{1}{5}x = \\frac{5}{10}x - \\frac{2}{10}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cb6c7b58110ede7a86ab979de95fcd7da981adb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"38\" /> and the area covered by the daisies on Rashid's portion would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e94aea6ca48fbab06e28dbe0dfa63619ccc6f74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}x - \\frac{3}{10}x = \\frac{4}{10}x - \\frac{3}{10}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"192\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd404bdbc8b56c121013bafdcd8e7207ed97060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{10}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"38\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of the area covered by the tulips on Rashid's portion.\n</p><p>Thus, the ratio of the number of daisies to the number of tulips on Rashid's portion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08da6a3aafa43c2360496bc38f9073fd173be063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"46\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC\">2025 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" ro